            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Years and Education</strong><br>\nMilton Friedman was born on July 31, 1912, in Brooklyn, New York. He earned his undergraduate degree from Rutgers University and received a Ph.D. in economics from Columbia University in 1946.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rise to Prominence</strong><br>\nFriedman became one of the most influential economists of the 20th century while teaching at the University of Chicago. He challenged many of the prevailing Keynesian economic policies with his strong advocacy for free-market principles.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Free Market Theory</strong><br>\nHe argued for the reduction of government intervention in the economy and promoted the use of monetary policy as a tool for managing economic stability. His ideas reshaped conservative economic policies, particularly in the 1970s and 1980s.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Nobel Prize in Economics</strong><br>\nFriedman was awarded the Nobel Prize in Economics in 1976 for his achievements in the fields of consumption analysis, monetary history, and theory, and for his demonstration of the complexity of stabilization policy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Influence</strong><br>\nHis political philosophy extended to his advising roles for U.S. Presidents and the British government, advocating for free-market economic policies, lower taxes, and a reduction in government spending.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Published Works</strong><br>\nFriedman authored several influential books, including \"Capitalism and Freedom\" (1962) and \"Free to Choose\" (1980), which argued that economic freedom was a necessary condition for political freedom.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
